From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] server: a zero-timeout mailslot read with nothing queued fails at once with STATUS_IO_TIMEOUT (3614)

server: a zero-timeout mailslot read with nothing queued fails at once with STATUS_IO_TIMEOUT

CORE: integrator must review.
Since 0798 the mailslot handle is asynchronous, so a read with a zero read timeout and no
message queued an async that timed out immediately: NtReadFile returned STATUS_PENDING and
filled the IO_STATUS_BLOCK later, where Windows (mailslot.c:113-115) returns STATUS_IO_TIMEOUT
from the call and leaves the block alone. mailslot_read now fails the request before queueing
when the timeout is zero and no message is waiting. Reads with a timeout, with a message, and
completion-port use (0798, test/mailslot-gate.sh) are unchanged.
---
diff --git a/server/mailslot.c b/server/mailslot.c
index b14954a..1ffa664 100644
--- a/server/mailslot.c
+++ b/server/mailslot.c
@@ -339,6 +339,14 @@ static void mailslot_read( struct fd *fd, struct async *async, file_pos_t pos )
 {
     struct mailslot *mailslot = get_fd_user( fd );
 
+    /* a zero timeout with nothing to read fails the request itself, before anything is queued */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_MAILSLOT_ZERO_ASYNC
+    if (!mailslot->read_timeout && !get_first_message( mailslot ))
+    {
+        set_error( STATUS_IO_TIMEOUT );
+        return;
+    }
+#endif
     if (mailslot->read_timeout != (timeout_t)-1)
         async_set_timeout( async, mailslot->read_timeout ? mailslot->read_timeout : -1, STATUS_IO_TIMEOUT );
     queue_async( &mailslot->read_q, async );
